  "description": "The one-call boot of a fresh install (no token, nothing cached) on a product whose registration is open (Config only, D-08). boot() fetches discovery, finds registration open and no token held, registers keylessly with a hashed fingerprint and stores the token, then runs its sync pass: the trust manifest, the config document (the product runs no licence service) and the report. The stage machine ends at its terminal outcome, ready: the gate's not-applicable passes, Update is off so nothing is decided, and no content stamp means nothing is fetched or mounted.",
